@using ALDevToolbox.Services.Palette

@*
    How a page tells the command palette what it is about. One hidden element,
    rendered by the page itself, that wwwroot/command-palette.js looks up each
    time the palette opens - so it is right after an enhanced navigation (the
    page's DOM is swapped, and the lookup happens after) and on a static page
    alike, and the palette never has to read the address to work it out.

    data-palette-context is handed to GET /palette/context verbatim; only the
    server reads it. data-palette-href is the record's own page, which the
    script remembers as a visit and leaves out of Recent while you are on it.
    See .design/command-palette.md, "Where you are".

    Rendered from the route parameter, not from the loaded record: a page for a
    record the caller cannot open still says what it is, and the server answers
    that with no context at all.
*@
<span hidden data-palette-context="@_reference.ToString()" data-palette-href="@_reference.Href"></span>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public PaletteContextKind Kind { get; set; }

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public int Id { get; set; }

    private PaletteContextRef _reference;

    protected override void OnParametersSet() => _reference = new PaletteContextRef(Kind, Id);
}
